From 792b33ed2dbdc03201e42ddf264c75b09854cd17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Brewka <oliver.brewka@9elements.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 16:23:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix platform_init service file description

The description is wrong and logs do not form properly. Fix the unit
description as per systemd docs [1].

Tested: Build a meta-catalina image.
Verify the systemd logs are formed correctly:

```
Mar 13 08:35:34 catalina systemd[1]: Starting initializing the platform hardware...
Mar 13 08:35:35 catalina platform-init[605]: Catalina platform init
Mar 13 08:35:39 catalina systemd[1]: Started initializing the platform hardware.
Mar 13 08:35:40 catalina systemd[1]: platform_init.service: Deactivated successfully.

```

[1] https://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/latest/systemd.unit.html#%5BUnit%5D%20Section%20Options

Gerrit: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/platform-init/+/91320/6

Change-Id: Id314dc9a9691ec0894b1e8452e46e6aed01c6824
Signed-off-by: Oliver Brewka <oliver.brewka@9elements.com>
---
 platform_init.service.in | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/platform_init.service.in b/platform_init.service.in
index 5c6d77f..d5bae53 100644
--- a/platform_init.service.in
+++ b/platform_init.service.in
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 [Unit]
-Description=Start up the platform hardware
+Description=init of platform hardware
 Before=xyz.openbmc_project.FruDevice.service
 
 [Service]
-- 
2.53.1-Meta

